module tasks.`2026-11-21-inbox-race-test-stall`

task InboxRaceTestStall {
  title "Flake: gui_inbox_question_race_and_retry_cross_real_sockets stalls past its 20 s window in the full mux run (0.2-0.6 s alone)"
  verify $ for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-term-mux --test it -E 'test(gui_inbox)' || exit 1; done
  paths "crates/bbt-mux"
  brief """
    Our stand: find the cause; do not widen the window or retry it away.

    ## Evidence (Oracle, 2026-11-21 06:20)
    - `make land` of rust-1-100 (`0ff6caba8`, which does not touch this test): 817/818 passed; `gui_endpoint::gui_inbox_question_race_and_retry_cross_real_sockets` failed twice (`TRY 2 FAIL [21.390s]`), panicking at `crates/bbt-mux/tests/gui_endpoint.rs:358` "missing GUI inbox event: Elapsed(())" (20 s `until` window, `:338`). Log: `~/mydev/bbx-rust-1-100/target/oracle-land.log:862`.
    - Alone on the same source: 3/3 passed in 0.29 s, 0.62 s, 0.19 s. Load ~6.7 with another executor building.
    - The test uses `tempfile::tempdir_in("/tmp")` and real sockets; check for socket-path or fixture-name collisions with concurrently running tests, an event subscription racing the first QuestionOpened (subscribe-then-page ordering), and a lost wake on the event lane.

    ## Do
    Reproduce under the full parallel run (or with a parallel stress loop), find the stall, fix the cause (ordering, unique paths), keep the 20 s hang guard. Add the failing interleaving as a deterministic test if it is an ordering bug.
  """

